      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T03:28:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As mentioned in another submission of this: It seems like this could be similarly enabled via setting pm_debug_messages in the boot arguments. Is there a stronger rationale for adding a vendor hook for this?",
      "revId": "d5bc54642cc1f9b99c18e73e4402fc45b25d3e3d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "45ac441f_6346d313",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T03:50:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also, as a minor nit, should this have the Change-Id: as Ief3d4196ea7220d4897c00a37ab96f456dbf2259 so it\u0027s clear it\u0027s a cherry-pick?",
      "revId": "d5bc54642cc1f9b99c18e73e4402fc45b25d3e3d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a555421_2f336936",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1241955
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T04:22:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "pm_debug_messages is much too coarse; it enables a large amount of log output during every suspend/resume cycle of which at most 1 line is helpful for investigating this recurring class of battery life issues.  Deploying builds with pm_debug_messages is therefore not viable, as it substantially shortens the temporal span of the log.  The new vendor hook will only emit logs specific to this class of problem, and only when the problem actually manifests.\n\ntl;dr - the new hook is a scalpel alternative to the pm_debug_messages chainsaw.",
      "parentUuid": "91af0e5a_454fcaf6",
      "revId": "d5bc54642cc1f9b99c18e73e4402fc45b25d3e3d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c7037f58_3fbea684",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T04:31:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, thanks for the extra context! I appreciate it!\n\nWould it make sense to just enable the specific log output generally? Or create a new boot option that would be available on all GKI kernels? Or maybe allow pm_debug_messages to have verbosity levels?\n\nI\u0027m mostly just concerned with adding more vendor-hook tech-debt instead of trying for a more general solution that has the potential to be upstreamed.",
      "parentUuid": "3a555421_2f336936",
      "revId": "d5bc54642cc1f9b99c18e73e4402fc45b25d3e3d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8f499d5b_21878e62",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1241955
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T05:32:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Over a handful of years working on battery life, one of the lessons I\u0027ve learned is: no matter how useful I may think a particular log message is, somebody else will have a good reason for disabling it.  :-)  So hard-enabling the logging of un-freezing tasks is something I\u0027m hesitant to do, no matter how beneficial and targeted it seems to me.\n\nAs for the mechanism, here\u0027s my thought process behind using a vendor hook:\n1) There are already two other vendor hooks in the same vicinity that target the same class of problems (but in different ways), and I believe the new hook complements those.\n2) One of those existing vendor hooks - `trace_android_vh_try_to_freeze_todo_unfrozen()` - isn\u0027t even called unless `pm_debug_messages` is enabled; you can\u0027t use it unless you enable the \"chainsaw\" log output that I referenced.  A side effect of this new hook is improving the utility of that _existing_ hook by allowing you to use it _without_ turning on `pm_debug_messages`.\n\nSo in very few lines of code:\n* it preserves choice for all GKI users\n* it fixes a significant shortcoming with one of the existing hooks\n\nI\u0027m not sure `pm_debug_messages` verbosity levels would work, as the log output it generates consists of a few roughly orthogonal categories rather than levels of detail.  As for a boot option, that would leave one of the existing hooks in its current ineffective state.",
      "parentUuid": "c7037f58_3fbea684",
      "revId": "d5bc54642cc1f9b99c18e73e4402fc45b25d3e3d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d26132e0_5f1f20fe",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1945845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T06:12:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e As for the mechanism, here\u0027s my thought process behind using a vendor hook:\n\u003e 1) There are already two other vendor hooks in the same vicinity that target the same class of problems (but in different ways), and I believe the new hook complements those.\n\nApologies if I\u0027m missing something, but it seems like one could also view it as redundant to trace_android_vh_try_to_freeze_todo() below this, as it looks like the logic in the if (pm_debug_messages_on) conditional, including the trace_android_vh_try_to_freeze_todo_unfrozen() could also be re-implemented within the trace_android_vh_try_to_freeze_todo_unfrozen hook?\n\n\n\u003e 2) One of those existing vendor hooks - `trace_android_vh_try_to_freeze_todo_unfrozen()` - isn\u0027t even called unless `pm_debug_messages` is enabled; you can\u0027t use it unless you enable the \"chainsaw\" log output that I referenced.  A side effect of this new hook is improving the utility of that _existing_ hook by allowing you to use it _without_ turning on `pm_debug_messages`.\n\u003e \n\nYeah, the _freeze_todo_unfrozen() hook seems a bit odd being inaccessible. \n\n\n\u003e I\u0027m not sure `pm_debug_messages` verbosity levels would work, as the log output it generates consists of a few roughly orthogonal categories rather than levels of detail.\n\nI\u0027m not the biggest fan of the approach, but some boot options use bitflags (like drm_debug) to provide similar fine grained control.\n\n\n\u003e As for a boot option, that would leave one of the existing hooks in its current ineffective state.\n\nFor this, my thought is the new boot option would be similar/equivalent to the vendor hook, enabling the single conditional.\n\nRegardless of my concerns here, I really appreciate the time for sharing the extra background context. I might ask that you provide some of the additional rationale in the commit message of the patch, as 5 years down the line this discussion will be hard to find.\n\nThanks again",
      "parentUuid": "8f499d5b_21878e62",
      "revId": "d5bc54642cc1f9b99c18e73e4402fc45b25d3e3d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
